-- title:
--   Galois S-level Fsupseteq L' with p-th power norm relation
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of rational primes with $p\in S$, and $L'$ an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ which is a number field, Galois over $\mathbb Q$, and unramified outside $S$ in the sense of the project predicate: $L'$ is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb Q$ and for every rational prime $q\notin S$ and every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ lies in the fixing subgroup of $L'$. Assume moreover that $L'$ contains an element $\zeta$ which is a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Then there exist an intermediate field $F$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ with $L'\le F$, a number-field and $\mathbb Q$-Galois structure on $F$, such that: $F$ is unramified outside $S$ in the same sense; $p$ divides the rank of $F$ as a module over $L'$ (via `extendScalars`, i.e. $p\mid [F:L']$); and for every idèle Galois descent datum $D$ for $F/\mathbb Q$ — a continuous monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(F/\mathbb Q)$ to the ring automorphisms of the adèle ring of $\mathcal O_F$ compatible with the action on $F$ — which stabilises the subgroup of unit idèles trivial on the height-one primes of $\mathcal O_F$ lying over the primes of $S$, and for every class $c$ in the corresponding $S$-idèle class group (the idèles modulo the subgroup generated by principal idèles together with those unit idèles trivial on that set of places), there is a class $d$ in the same group which is fixed by the induced action `sClassAct` of every element of the fixing subgroup $H$ of the image of $L'$ in $F$, and such that $\prod_{g\in H} D.\mathrm{sClassAct}(g)\,c = d^{p}$.
--
--   This is the norm form of the existence theorem of global class field theory, packaged at a Galois level $F$ of the tower inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ that is unramified outside $S$: the $\mathrm{Gal}(F/L')$-norm of every $S$-idèle class is a $p$-th power of an invariant class. It is shaped so as to supply the norm hypothesis in the cohomological level-raising step, and is used in the construction of levels for relation homomorphisms on $S$-idèle class groups.
